{"seconds": 53.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Yes, the rook is on g6 and can capture the pawn on g7 with check. The best move is **Rxg7+**.\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nWhen your rook and queen coordinate on the kingside and your opponent's king is trapped, look for forcing checks. Here, Rxg7+ removes the pawn shield and forces the king into the open. After Kxg7, Qh8+ drives it further, and Kf7 allows you to win the rook with Qxf8+. The lesson: sacrificing material to expose a king often wins it back decisively with advantage. Always check if your attacking pieces can coordinate to deliver this kind of knockout.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rxg7+\", \"line\": [\"Rxg7+\", \"Kxg7\", \"Qh8+\", \"Kf7\", \"Qxf8+\", \"Kg6\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/pp1b2p1/4p1R1/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 w - - 0 29"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/pp1b2p1/4p1R1/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 w - - 0 29"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/pp1b2p1/4p1R1/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 w - - 0 29"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/pp1b2p1/4p1R1/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 w - - 0 29", "move": "Qh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/pp1b2p1/4p1R1/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 w - - 0 29", "move": "Qh7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/pp1b2p1/4p1R1/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 w - - 0 29", "move": "Rxg7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/pp1b2R1/4p3/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 b - - 0 29", "move": "Kxg7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r2/pp1b2k1/4p3/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 w - - 0 30", "move": "Qh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r2/pp1b2k1/4p3/3pP2Q/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2KR4 w - - 0 30", "move": "Qg6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r2/pp1b2k1/4p1Q1/3pP3/3P4/8/qP1N1r2/2